6. Relationship to upstream RimWorld Together
---------------------------------------------

The Work interoperates with the RimWorld Together mod ("RWT") at
runtime via published APIs and well-documented protocols. The Work
contains NONE of RWT's source code, defs, assets, or compiled
binaries. RWT remains the property of its respective authors under
its own license (Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-
NoDerivatives 4.0 International). This License governs only the
Work and does not modify, override, or supersede RWT's license in
any way.


7. Extensions via the public SDK
--------------------------------

Use of the publicly documented `KMH.Sdk.Server` namespace (and any
future `KMH.Sdk.Client` namespace) from a separately distributed
extension assembly is permitted and is not considered a
modification of the Work for purposes of Section 2.

This permission covers:

  - Writing extensions that reference the SDK's public interfaces,
    records, and event payloads
  - Distributing such extensions under any license the author
    chooses (including commercial / closed-source)
  - Bundling multiple SDK-using extensions together

This permission does NOT cover:

  - Modifying, forking, or redistributing the Work's own source or
    binaries (those still require permission per Section 2)
  - Bundling KMH binaries inside an extension distribution —
    extensions must direct users to obtain KMH from the upstream
    official release

See EXTENSIONS.md in the project root for the SDK reference and
the contract-stability policy that protects extension authors from
KMH internal changes between releases.


